00:00:45.089 --> 00:00:49.219
whole idea that collisions had to be
made, and they had molecules had to be

00:00:49.259 --> 00:00:54.300
oriented the right way, and there had to
be activation energy that was required

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.849
for these different reactions to happen.

00:00:56.159 --> 00:01:00.110
So you kind of learn that, okay,
concentration, temperature, uh,

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:03.230
depending on how much energy there
is, the pressure, the volume,

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.089
all these conditions play a role.

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:09.195
which is where we were really seeing
that, okay, well, we can try to, we can

00:01:09.264 --> 00:01:13.695
essentially poke this different, this
metaphorical equilibrium beast with

00:01:13.695 --> 00:01:16.844
a stick and see like, all right, how
is it exactly going to react to that?

00:01:17.315 --> 00:01:20.124
And then we also learned about all
the different acids and bases and

00:01:20.124 --> 00:01:23.874
how this different strengths play a
big role behind all of that as well.

00:01:24.414 --> 00:01:28.334
Now, when we learn about all that,
that all kind of gets put together

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:33.645
into this concept of the K expression,
which is an equilibrium expression.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:38.800
Where if you have a balanced chemical
